"Am" A3 B e4 | "G" d3 B d4 | "Bm" B3 A G2 g2 | "Am" f2 g2 a4 |
w: Ca' the ewes to the knowes, Ca' them whaur the hea-ther grows,
"Em" b3 e e2 e2 | "Bm" d2 g2 B4 | "Am" A4 "Bm" B3 d | "Em" e4 e2 z2 |
w: Ca' them whaur' the bur-nie grows, My bon-nie dear-ie.
"Am" A3 B e3 e | "G" d3 B d4 | "Bm" B3 A G2 g2 | "Am" f2 g2 a4 |
w: Hark, the mav-is ev'n-in' song, Sound-in' Clu-den's woods a-mang,
"Em" b3 e e3 e | "Bm" d2 g2 B4 | "Am" A4 "Bm" B3 d | "Em" e4 e2 z2 |]
w: Then a-fauld-in' let us gang, My bon-nie dear-ie.
%
% %leftmargin 1.5in
W: 1. Ca' the ewes to the knowes, Ca' them whaur' the heather grows,
W: Ca' them whaur' the burnie grows, my bonnie dearie.
W:
W: 2. We'll gae down by Cluden side, Through the hazels spreading wide,
W: O'er the waves that sweetly glide, to the moon sae clearly.
W:
W: 3. Fair and lovely as though art, Though has stown my very heart:
W: I can die, but canna part, My Bonnie dearie.
W:
W: 4. Ca' the ewes to the knowes, Ca' them whaur' the heather grows,
W: Ca' them whaur' the burnie grows, my bonnie dearie.
